  "text": "We replace $p$ with $5$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p}{10}+\\frac{1}{p}= \\\\ \\frac{3(5)}{10}+\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{10}+\\frac{1}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{10}+\\frac{2}{10} & = \\\\ \\frac{15+2}{10} & = \\\\ \\frac{17}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
